b.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-06T03:52:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-06T03:54:11Z","body":"> To be clear, are you in the scene or the sub-scene?\r\n> \r\n> As far as I know, the outer scene saves the changes to the subscene or the outer scene change should be disallowed. The subscene should be bit-exact from a version control point of view.\r\n\r\nIn the scene test4.\r\nI doubt `the outer scene saves the changes to the subscene or the outer scene change should be disallowed`. You can see that in `test3.tscn`, the modified value of test1's property `map` and `property1` is saved in `test3.tscn` file:\r\n```\r\n[node name=\"test1\" parent=\"test_2\" index=\"0\"]\r\nmap = {\r\n\"fff\": 121,\r\n\"ggg\": 666\r\n}\r\nproperty1 = 2\r\n```\r\nand in `test4.tscn`, you can see that the modified value of test1's property `property1` is saved in `test4.tscn` file:\r\n```\r\n[node name=\"test1\" parent=\"test_3/test_2\" index=\"0\"]\r\nproperty1 = 2304197747\r\n```\r\nwhich means outer scene can save it's modification on the sub-scene's exported property because I enabled sub-scene's `Editable Children` function.\r\n<img width=\"366\" alt=\"屏幕截图 2024-11-06 114659\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/419ce882-c125-4eec-8950-ec68e228cd37\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> I think it's somehow a bug in the `export_tool_button, but I am unsure.\r\n\r\nIt's not a bug of export_tool_button because I add this to test4.gd to modify test1's map without using export_tool_button but still the value is not saved in tscn file:\r\n```\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tawait get_tree().create_timer(2).timeout\r\n\ttest() # add a new key/value to map\r\n\ttest() # add a new key/value to map\r\n\ttest() # add a new key/value to map\r\n\ttest() # add a new key/value to map\r\n\tprintt(\"finish and save manually.\")\r\n\t\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2458674713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]